msgid "Connect the UART from the 'Customer Interface' port on the fuel cell to any serial port on your autopilot.  `See device user manual <https://www.intelligent-energy.com/our-products/support/>`__ for details on where to find the 'Customer Interface'.  Only the GND, UART TX, and UART RX connections are required.  See the diagram below:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie650-fuelcell.rst:33
#: 5cd9163a057f43bcb3845e8ffb3de6ac
msgid "Parameter Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie650-fuelcell.rst:35
#: 8461e80b707d490db11ffdd83b716f5b
msgid "Enable the fuel cell driver by setting :ref:`GEN_TYPE <GEN_TYPE>` to 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie650-fuelcell.rst:37
#: 9673861ecfff42e5aa5cebf9a4143f70
msgid "Fuel cell telemetry is transmitted over serial.  The appropriate serial port needs to be configured to receive fuel cell data.  Set the :ref:`SERIALX_PROTOCOL <SERIAL1_PROTOCOL>` parameter to 30 for generator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie650-fuelcell.rst:39
#: 4c42967bd40944459687a131051461f4
msgid "The generator library utilises the battery monitor mavlink message to display fuel cell telemetry on the ground station.  Two battery monitor instances are required for one fuel cell.  One for the fuel tank and another for the battery.  Set :ref:`BATTX_MONITOR <BATT_MONITOR>` parameter to 17 for the fuel cells electrical data.  Set another :ref:`BATTX_MONITOR <BATT_MONITOR>` parameter to 18 for the hydrogen tank telemetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie650-fuelcell.rst:41
#: 99e80de1e5264085ac36b81f20a6b369
msgid "This fuel cell unit only reports battery percentage remaining and tank percentage remaining.  As such, the following parameters must be set for both tank and battery:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie650-fuelcell.rst:43
#: 188fabdde093490fbf47875ddab29918
msgid ":ref:`BATTX_CAPACITY <BATT_CAPACITY>` = 100 must be set to give a sensible readout of a percentage on the GCS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie650-fuelcell.rst:45
#: 9339b87b89d24d4fa2525c994d4761e9
msgid "Capacity related failsafes can be set using :ref:`BATTX_LOW_MAH <BATT_LOW_MAH>`, :ref:`BATTX_CRT_MAH <BATT_CRT_MAH>`, :ref:`BATTX_ARM_MAH <BATT_ARM_MAH>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie650-fuelcell.rst:47
#: bff7e0a69ec546ddb8661d8fbea52108
msgid "Reboot the autopilot after setting the parameters for the settings to take effect."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie650-fuelcell.rst:50
#: 1d58787b417a44da8f52c5952ea0f343
msgid "In this instance, ignore the units of these parameters.  The capacities are only reported as a percentage.  As such values should be entered in the range from 1 to 100."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ie650-fuelcell.rst:53
#: ea024205d8124bc3ad920cdee5501290
msgid "No voltage data is available for these units and a fixed voltage of 1 V is always reported.  To avoid low voltage pre-arm warnings and failsafes :ref:`BATTX_ARM_VOLT <BATT_ARM_VOLT>` = 0, :ref:`BATTX_LOW_VOLT <BATT_LOW_VOLT>` = 0, and :ref:`BATTX_CRT_VOLT <BATT_CRT_VOLT>` = 0 must be set to disable voltage related failsafes on this model."
msgstr ""

